+  // =========================================================================
+  // REBOOT (IEEE 1722.1-2021 §7.4.43; issue #203): the SUCCESS response, the
+  // REBOOT's notifications and ENTITY_DEPARTING leave, then reboot_req_o, and
+  // no frame follows until reset
+  // =========================================================================
+  //! Every wait reads the TX output itself: a frame has left when the MAC
+  //! takes its last byte. Grants are frame-atomic and only an idle arbiter
+  //! grants, so the frame in flight is the last one granted, of a known lane.
+  //!  - RB_RESP: aecp_reboot_w rises the clock after the SUCCESS response's
+  //!    grant, so the next last byte is that response's.
+  //!  - RB_NTF: the REBOOT's notification (class 9, every registered
+  //!    controller but the requester: §7.5.2, Milan v1.2 §5.4.5.2) is queued
+  //!    before the response is built, and each job retires at its grant, so
+  //!    once the notify block holds no command work and no unsolicited frame
+  //!    is in flight, the last one has left. Notifications of other kinds may
+  //!    follow; nothing waits for them.
+  //!  - RB_DOWN: one clock with ADP's enable fallen, Milan v1.2's SHUTDOWN:
+  //!    each advertise machine not DOWN queues ENTITY_DEPARTING
+  //!    (§5.6.3.5.8, §5.6.3.5.11; IEEE §6.2.4 doTerminate, §6.2.5.2.2); a
+  //!    DOWN one, not advertising, sends none (Table 5.51).
+  //!  - RB_DEP: ADP has nothing left to build or queue, and the arbiter is
+  //!    idle (REQ-FWX-001): the last frame it started, of any lane, has
+  //!    left. That is the last DEPARTING when the entity advertised. A frame
+  //!    another lane had selected before the transmit gate closed (a lock
+  //!    expiry's notification, a listener's probe) is sent whole first, with
+  //!    or without a DEPARTING. This exit is taken only with the gate closed
+  //!    and ADP's queue empty, so no frame is being selected either.
+  //!  - RB_REQ: reboot_req_o, held until rst_n.
+  //! The transmit gate (REQ-FWX-001): from the clock ADP has built and
+  //! queued its last ENTITY_DEPARTING (RB_DEP with ADP no longer busy) to
+  //! the reset, the arbiter starts no frame on any lane but ADP's, and ADP,
+  //! its enable fallen for good, builds nothing more, so after the final
+  //! DEPARTING the entity is silent. That holds the producers that keep
+  //! running while the integrator withholds the reset: lock expiry and every
+  //! other AECP notification, CONTROLLER_AVAILABLE, the listener's probes,
+  //! MAAP and SRP. The answering lanes are closed too, though no command
+  //! reaches them. The gate waits for the DEPARTINGs to be built because ADP
+  //! builds into the shared TX slots and a producer held at the gate keeps
+  //! its slot: closed at the SHUTDOWN, frames already waiting could hold
+  //! every slot and leave none for the DEPARTING. Until it closes every lane
+  //! drains, ahead of the DEPARTINGs, and RB_DEP waits for the frame it
+  //! closes on, so no frame is on tx_* from reboot_req_o's rise to the reset.
+  typedef enum logic [2:0] {
